IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc24-attendance.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part XXII (Procuring Attendance), sections 697 to 708.1:
-- Application, Process (subpoena and warrant), Execution or Service of Process, Defaulting or Absconding Witness, Contempt, Electronically Transmitted Copies.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), part agent ccc24. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of ccc24-appeal-procedure.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING; a caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE).
-- "The person" is a witness: the accused, or a person who may become the accused, is in the seat as a person served with a subpoena, held on a warrant or bound by a recognizance.
-- Answers named "the bar ... applies" answer JUST TRUE when the text's prohibition bites on the facts, JUST FALSE where its own exception or fixed period takes the case out of it, and NOTHING where the prohibition is not engaged.

§ `Part XXII -- Procuring Attendance (sections 697 to 708.1)`

§§ `Section 697 -- Application`

-- src:14548 | 697 Except where section 527 applies, this Part applies where a person is required to attend to give evidence in a proceeding to which this Act applies.
@ref s 697 (src:14548-14548)
GIVEN `section 527 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person is required to attend to give evidence in a proceeding to which this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 697 Part XXII applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 527 applies`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where section 527 applies"
        IF `a person is required to attend to give evidence in a proceeding to which this Act applies`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this Part applies where a person is required to attend to give evidence in a proceeding to which this Act applies"

§§ `Section 698 -- Subpoena; warrant in Form 17`

-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14552 | 698 (1) Where a person is likely to give material evidence in a proceeding to which this Act applies, a subpoena may be issued in accordance with this Part requiring that person to attend to give evidence.
@ref s 698(1) (src:14552-14552)
GIVEN `the person is likely to give material evidence in a proceeding to which this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 698(1) a subpoena may be issued in accordance with Part XXII requiring the person to attend to give evidence` MEANS
    IF `the person is likely to give material evidence in a proceeding to which this Act applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is likely to give material evidence in a proceeding to which this Act applies"

-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14554 | (2) Where it is made to appear that a person who is likely to give material evidence
-- src:14555 | (a) will not attend in response to a subpoena if a subpoena is issued, or
-- src:14556 | (b) is evading service of a subpoena,
-- src:14557 | a court, justice or provincial court judge having power to issue a subpoena to require the attendance of that person to give evidence may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause that person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence.
@ref s 698(2) (src:14554-14557)
GIVEN `the person is likely to give material evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made to appear that the person will not attend in response to a subpoena if a subpoena is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made to appear that the person is evading service of a subpoena` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer is a court, justice or provincial court judge having power to issue a subpoena to require the attendance of the person to give evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 698(2) a court, justice or provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause the person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence` MEANS
    IF    `the person is likely to give material evidence`
      AND (`it is made to appear that the person will not attend in response to a subpoena if a subpoena is issued` OR `it is made to appear that the person is evading service of a subpoena`)
      AND `the issuer is a court, justice or provincial court judge having power to issue a subpoena to require the attendance of the person to give evidence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is made to appear that a person who is likely to give material evidence"

-- 698(3): "shall not be issued unless a subpoena has first been issued", except where (2)(a) applies.
-- src:14559 | (3) Except where paragraph (2)(a) applies, a warrant in Form 17 shall not be issued unless a subpoena has first been issued.
@ref s 698(3) (src:14559-14559)
GIVEN `paragraph (2)(a) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a subpoena has first been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant in Form 17 is to be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 698(3) the bar on issuing a warrant in Form 17 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a warrant in Form 17 is to be issued`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a warrant in Form 17 shall not be issued"
        IF `paragraph (2)(a) applies`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where paragraph (2)(a) applies"
        IF `a subpoena has first been issued`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a subpoena has first been issued"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 699 -- Who may issue`

-- src:14561 | 699 (1) If a person is required to attend to give evidence before a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction other than a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX, a subpoena directed to that person shall be issued out of the court before which the attendance of that person is required.
@ref s 699(1) (src:14561-14561)
GIVEN `the person is required to attend to give evidence before a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction other than a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 699(1) the subpoena shall be issued out of the court before which the attendance of the person is required` MEANS
    IF `the person is required to attend to give evidence before a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction other than a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person is required to attend to give evidence before a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction other than a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX"

DECLARE `s 699(2) issuer` IS ONE OF
    `s 699(2)(a) a provincial court judge or a justice`
    `s 699(2)(b) a provincial court judge or a superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the proceedings were instituted`
    `s 699(2) another issuer`

-- "where the person whose attendance is required is within the province" (a) / "is not within the province" (b): where-gates, JUST FALSE where the gate fails (ruling (b)).
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14563 | (2) If a person is required to attend to give evidence before a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a summary conviction court under Part XXVII or in proceedings over which a justice has jurisdiction, a subpoena directed to the person shall be issued
-- src:14564 | (a) by a provincial court judge or a justice, where the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the proceedings were instituted; or
-- src:14565 | (b) by a provincial court judge or out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the proceedings were instituted, where the person whose attendance is required is not within the province.
@ref s 699(2) (src:14563-14565)
GIVEN issuer IS A `s 699(2) issuer`
      `the person is required to attend to give evidence before a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a summary conviction court under Part XXVII or in proceedings over which a justice has jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the proceedings were instituted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 699(2) the subpoena shall be issued by the issuer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is required to attend to give evidence before a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a summary conviction court under Part XXVII or in proceedings over which a justice has jurisdiction`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person is required to attend to give evidence before a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a summary conviction court under Part XXVII"
        IF issuer EQUALS `s 699(2) another issuer`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "a subpoena directed to the person shall be issued"
        IF issuer EQUALS `s 699(2)(a) a provincial court judge or a justice`
        THEN (IF `the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the proceedings were instituted` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the proceedings were instituted"
        OTHERWISE (IF NOT `the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the proceedings were instituted` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the person whose attendance is required is not within the province"

-- src:14567 | (3) A subpoena shall not be issued out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction pursuant to paragraph (2)(b), except pursuant to an order of a judge of the court made on application by a party to the proceedings.
@ref s 699(3) (src:14567-14567)
GIVEN `the subpoena is to be issued out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction pursuant to paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an order of a judge of the court made on application by a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 699(3) the bar on issuing a subpoena out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction pursuant to paragraph (2)(b) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the subpoena is to be issued out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction pursuant to paragraph (2)(b)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A subpoena shall not be issued out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction pursuant to paragraph (2)(b)"
        IF `there is an order of a judge of the court made on application by a party to the proceedings`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except pursuant to an order of a judge of the court made on application by a party to the proceedings"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:14569 | (4) A subpoena or warrant that is issued by a court under this Part shall be under the seal of the court and shall be signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court.
@ref s 699(4) (src:14569-14569)
GIVEN `the subpoena or warrant is issued by a court under Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena or warrant is under the seal of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena or warrant is signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 699(4) the subpoena or warrant is under the seal of the court and is signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court` MEANS
    IF `the subpoena or warrant is issued by a court under Part XXII` AND `the subpoena or warrant is under the seal of the court` AND `the subpoena or warrant is signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be under the seal of the court and shall be signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court"

-- src:14571 | (5) A subpoena or warrant that is issued by a justice or provincial court judge under this Part must be signed by the justice, provincial court judge or the clerk of the court.
@ref s 699(5) (src:14571-14571)
GIVEN `the subpoena or warrant is issued by a justice or provincial court judge under Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena or warrant is signed by the justice, provincial court judge or the clerk of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 699(5) the subpoena or warrant is signed by the justice, provincial court judge or the clerk of the court` MEANS
    IF `the subpoena or warrant is issued by a justice or provincial court judge under Part XXII` AND `the subpoena or warrant is signed by the justice, provincial court judge or the clerk of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be signed by the justice, provincial court judge or the clerk of the court"

-- src:14573 | (5.1) Despite anything in subsections (1) to (5), in the case of an offence referred to in section 278.11, a subpoena requiring a witness to bring to the court a record or a therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 must be issued by a judge and signed by the judge or the clerk of the court.
@ref s 699(5.1) (src:14573-14573)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence referred to in section 278.11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena requires a witness to bring to the court a record or a therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena is issued by a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena is signed by the judge or the clerk of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 699(5.1) the subpoena is issued by a judge and signed by the judge or the clerk of the court` MEANS
    IF `the offence is an offence referred to in section 278.11` AND `the subpoena requires a witness to bring to the court a record or a therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19` AND `the subpoena is issued by a judge` AND `the subpoena is signed by the judge or the clerk of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be issued by a judge and signed by the judge or the clerk of the court"

-- 699(6) "Subject to subsection (7), a subpoena issued under this Part may be in Form 16": in the (7) case the Form is 16.1, so Form 16 is then NOT COVERED.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14575 | (6) Subject to subsection (7), a subpoena issued under this Part may be in Form 16.
@ref s 699(6) (src:14575-14575)
GIVEN `the subpoena is issued under Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (7) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 699(6) the subpoena may be in Form 16` MEANS
    IF `the subpoena is issued under Part XXII` AND (NOT `subsection (7) applies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (7), a subpoena issued under this Part may be in Form 16"

-- src:14577 | (7) In the case of an offence referred to in section 278.11, a subpoena requiring a witness to bring anything to the court shall be in Form 16.1.
@ref s 699(7) (src:14577-14577)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence referred to in section 278.11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena requires a witness to bring anything to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena is in Form 16.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 699(7) the subpoena is in Form 16.1` MEANS
    IF `the offence is an offence referred to in section 278.11` AND `the subpoena requires a witness to bring anything to the court` AND `the subpoena is in Form 16.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of an offence referred to in section 278.11, a subpoena requiring a witness to bring anything to the court shall be in Form 16.1"

§§ `Section 700 -- Contents of subpoena; witness to appear and remain`

-- src:14579 | 700 (1) A subpoena shall require the person to whom it is directed to attend, at a time and place to be stated in the subpoena, to give evidence and, if required, to bring with him anything that he has in his possession or under his control relating to the subject-matter of the proceedings.
@ref s 700(1) (src:14579-14579)
GIVEN `the subpoena requires the person to whom it is directed to attend to give evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena states the time and place of attendance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 700(1) the subpoena requires the person to attend, at a time and place stated in the subpoena, to give evidence` MEANS
    IF `the subpoena requires the person to whom it is directed to attend to give evidence` AND `the subpoena states the time and place of attendance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A subpoena shall require the person to whom it is directed to attend, at a time and place to be stated in the subpoena, to give evidence"

-- src:14581 | (2) A person who is served with a subpoena issued under this Part shall attend and shall remain in attendance throughout the proceedings unless he is excused by the presiding judge, justice or provincial court judge.
@ref s 700(2) (src:14581-14581)
GIVEN `the person is served with a subpoena issued under Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is excused by the presiding judge, justice or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 700(2) the person must attend and remain in attendance throughout the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is served with a subpoena issued under Part XXII`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is served with a subpoena issued under this Part"
        IF `the person is excused by the presiding judge, justice or provincial court judge`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he is excused by the presiding judge, justice or provincial court judge"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 700.1 -- Video links`

-- src:14583 | 700.1 (1) If a person is to give evidence under section 714.1 or under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act — or is to give evidence or a statement under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act — at a place within the jurisdiction of a court referred to in subsection 699(1) or (2) where the technology is available, a subpoena shall be issued out of the court to order the person to give that evidence at that place.
@ref s 700.1(1) (src:14583-14583)
GIVEN `the person is to give evidence under section 714.1 or under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act or is to give evidence or a statement under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is within the jurisdiction of a court referred to in subsection 699(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technology is available at that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 700.1(1) a subpoena shall be issued out of the court to order the person to give the evidence at that place` MEANS
    IF `the person is to give evidence under section 714.1 or under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act or is to give evidence or a statement under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` AND `the place is within the jurisdiction of a court referred to in subsection 699(1) or (2)` AND `the technology is available at that place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person is to give evidence under section 714.1 or under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act"

-- src:14585 | (2) Sections 699, 700 and 701 to 703.2 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to a subpoena issued under this section.
@ref s 700.1(2) (src:14585-14585)
GIVEN `the section number` IS A NUMBER
      `the subpoena is issued under section 700.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` MEANS
    IF `the subpoena is issued under section 700.1` AND (`the section number` EQUALS 699 OR `the section number` EQUALS 700 OR (`the section number` AT LEAST 701 AND `the section number` AT MOST 703.2))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Sections 699, 700 and 701 to 703.2 apply"

§§ `Sections 701 to 703.2 -- Execution or service of process`

-- src:14589 | 701 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a subpoena shall be served in a province by a peace officer or any other person who is qualified in that province to serve civil process, in accordance with subsection 509(2), with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref s 701(1) (src:14589-14589)
GIVEN `the server is a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the server is another person who is qualified in the province to serve civil process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 701(1) the subpoena shall be served in a province by the server` MEANS
    IF `the server is a peace officer` OR `the server is another person who is qualified in the province to serve civil process`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by a peace officer or any other person who is qualified in that province to serve civil process"

-- src:14591 | (2) A subpoena that is issued pursuant to paragraph 699(2)(b) shall be served personally on the person to whom it is directed.
@ref s 701(2) (src:14591-14591)
GIVEN `the subpoena was issued pursuant to paragraph 699(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subpoena has been served personally on the person to whom it is directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 701(2) the subpoena has been served personally on the person to whom it is directed` MEANS
    IF `the subpoena was issued pursuant to paragraph 699(2)(b)` AND `the subpoena has been served personally on the person to whom it is directed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be served personally on the person to whom it is directed"

