DECLARE `s 703.2 organization` IS ONE OF
    `s 703.2(a) a municipality`
    `s 703.2(b) an organization other than a municipality`

-- "Where any summons ... is required to be or may be served on an organization, and no other method of service is provided": a where-gate on a grant, JUST FALSE where it fails (ruling (b)).
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14606 | 703.2 Where any summons, notice or other process is required to be or may be served on an organization, and no other method of service is provided, service may be effected by delivery
-- src:14607 | (a) in the case of a municipality, to the mayor, warden, reeve or other chief officer of the municipality, or to the secretary, treasurer or clerk of the municipality; and
-- src:14608 | (b) in the case of any other organization, to the manager, secretary or other senior officer of the organization or one of its branches.
@ref s 703.2 (src:14606-14608)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 703.2 organization`
      `a summons, notice or other process is required to be or may be served on the organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no other method of service is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delivery is to the mayor, warden, reeve or other chief officer of the municipality, or to the secretary, treasurer or clerk of the municipality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delivery is to the manager, secretary or other senior officer of the organization or one of its branches` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 703.2 service may be effected by delivery to the officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a summons, notice or other process is required to be or may be served on the organization` AND `no other method of service is provided`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any summons, notice or other process is required to be or may be served on an organization, and no other method of service is provided"
        IF kind EQUALS `s 703.2(a) a municipality`
        THEN (IF `the delivery is to the mayor, warden, reeve or other chief officer of the municipality, or to the secretary, treasurer or clerk of the municipality` THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a municipality, to the mayor, warden, reeve or other chief officer of the municipality, or to the secretary, treasurer or clerk of the municipality"
        OTHERWISE (IF `the delivery is to the manager, secretary or other senior officer of the organization or one of its branches` THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of any other organization, to the manager, secretary or other senior officer of the organization or one of its branches"

§§ `Sections 704 to 707 -- Defaulting or absconding witness`

-- 704(1): "Where a person is bound by recognizance" is a where-gate (JUST FALSE where it fails); "a justice who is satisfied on information ... in writing and under oath" names who may.
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14612 | 704 (1) Where a person is bound by recognizance to give evidence in any proceedings, a justice who is satisfied on information being made before him in writing and under oath that the person is about to abscond or has absconded may issue his warrant in Form 18 directing a peace officer to arrest that person and to bring him before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom he is bound to appear.
@ref s 704(1) (src:14612-14612)
GIVEN `the person is bound by recognizance to give evidence in any proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a justice is satisfied on information made before the justice in writing and under oath that the person is about to abscond or has absconded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 704(1) the justice may issue a warrant in Form 18 directing a peace officer to arrest the person and to bring the person before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person is bound to appear` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is bound by recognizance to give evidence in any proceedings`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is bound by recognizance to give evidence in any proceedings"
        IF `a justice is satisfied on information made before the justice in writing and under oath that the person is about to abscond or has absconded`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a justice who is satisfied on information being made before him in writing and under oath that the person is about to abscond or has absconded"

-- src:14614 | (2) Section 528 applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to a warrant issued under this section.
@ref s 704(2) (src:14614-14614)
GIVEN `the warrant is issued under section 704` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 704(2) section 528 applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the warrant is issued under section 704`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 528 applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to a warrant issued under this section"

-- 704(3): "entitled, on request": an "entitled" function, listed for a lawyer; an on-gate that fails is JUST FALSE (ruling (b)).
-- @tag grant=entitled
-- src:14616 | (3) A person who is arrested under this section is entitled, on request, to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for his arrest was issued.
@ref s 704(3) (src:14616-14616)
GIVEN `the person is arrested under section 704` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has requested a copy of the information on which the warrant for the arrest was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 704(3) the person is entitled to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for the arrest was issued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is arrested under section 704`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is arrested under this section"
        IF NOT `the person has requested a copy of the information on which the warrant for the arrest was issued`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on request, to receive a copy of the information"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14618 | 705 (1) If a person who has been served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding does not attend or remain in attendance, the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom that person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of that person if it is established
-- src:14619 | (a) that the subpoena has been served in accordance with this Part, and
-- src:14620 | (b) that the person is likely to give material evidence.
@ref s 705(1) (src:14618-14620)
GIVEN `the person has been served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not attend or remain in attendance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established that the subpoena has been served in accordance with Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established that the person is likely to give material evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 705(1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has been served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding` AND `the person does not attend or remain in attendance` AND `it is established that the subpoena has been served in accordance with Part XXII` AND `it is established that the person is likely to give material evidence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of that person if it is established"

-- @tag grant=flip
