-- 705.1(7): "remain in effect until they are cancelled or changed or until the person appears and remains in attendance": an until-bar (ruling (d)): JUST FALSE after the event.
-- src:14648 | (7) The conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect until they are cancelled or changed or until the person appears and remains in attendance at the proceeding as required by the mandatory condition.
@ref s 705.1(7) (src:14648-14648)
GIVEN `an undertaking has been given under section 705.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions have been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions have been changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has appeared and remained in attendance at the proceeding as required by the mandatory condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 705.1(7) the conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an undertaking has been given under section 705.1`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The conditions with respect to the undertaking"
        IF `the conditions have been cancelled` OR `the conditions have been changed` OR `the person has appeared and remained in attendance at the proceeding as required by the mandatory condition`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until they are cancelled or changed or until the person appears and remains in attendance at the proceeding"
