DECLARE `s 706 order` IS ONE OF
    `s 706 order that the person be detained in custody`
    `s 706 order that the person be released on recognizance with sureties`
    `s 706 order that the person be released on recognizance without sureties`
    `s 706 another order`

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14650 | 706 If a person is brought before a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice under a warrant issued under subsection 698(2) or section 704 or 705, the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may, so that the person will appear and give evidence when required, order that the person be detained in custody or be released on recognizance, with or without sureties.
@ref s 706 (src:14650-14650)
GIVEN order IS A `s 706 order`
      `the person is brought before a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice under a warrant issued under subsection 698(2) or section 704 or 705` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made so that the person will appear and give evidence when required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order` MEANS
    IF order EQUALS `s 706 another order`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may, so that the person will appear and give evidence when required, order that the person be detained in custody or be released on recognizance, with or without sureties"
    ELSE IF `the person is brought before a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice under a warrant issued under subsection 698(2) or section 704 or 705` AND `the order is made so that the person will appear and give evidence when required`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person is brought before a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice under a warrant issued under subsection 698(2) or section 704 or 705"

-- 707(1): "No person shall be detained in custody ... for the purpose only of appearing and giving evidence when required as a witness, for any period exceeding thirty days
-- unless prior to the expiration of those thirty days he has been brought before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the province in which he is being detained."
-- JUST TRUE = the bar bites (more than thirty days, no such judge); JUST FALSE = within the thirty days, or brought before that judge in time ("unless").
-- src:14652 | 707 (1) No person shall be detained in custody under the authority of any provision of this Act, for the purpose only of appearing and giving evidence when required as a witness, for any period exceeding thirty days unless prior to the expiration of those thirty days he has been brought before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the province in which he is being detained.
@ref s 707(1) (src:14652-14652)
GIVEN `the person is detained in custody for the purpose only of appearing and giving evidence when required as a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of detention` IS A NUMBER
      `the person was brought before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the province in which the person is being detained before the expiration of the thirty days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 707(1) the bar on detaining a witness for more than thirty days applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is detained in custody for the purpose only of appearing and giving evidence when required as a witness`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose only of appearing and giving evidence when required as a witness"
        IF `the person was brought before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the province in which the person is being detained before the expiration of the thirty days`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless prior to the expiration of those thirty days he has been brought before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction"
        IF `the number of days of detention` AT MOST 30
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for any period exceeding thirty days"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:14654 | (2) Where at any time prior to the expiration of the thirty days referred to in subsection (1), a witness being detained in custody as described in that subsection applies to be brought before a judge of a court described therein, the judge before whom the application is brought shall fix a time prior to the expiration of those thirty days for the hearing of the application and shall cause notice of the time so fixed to be given to the witness, the person having custody of the witness and such other persons as the judge may specify, and at the time so fixed for the hearing of the application the person having custody of the witness shall cause the witness to be brought before a judge of the court for that purpose.
@ref s 707(2) (src:14654-14654)
GIVEN `the witness is detained in custody as described in subsection 707(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness applies to be brought before a judge of a court described in subsection 707(1) before the expiration of the thirty days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 707(2) the judge must fix a time before the expiration of the thirty days for the hearing of the application and cause notice of it to be given, and the person having custody of the witness must cause the witness to be brought before a judge` MEANS
    IF `the witness is detained in custody as described in subsection 707(1)` AND `the witness applies to be brought before a judge of a court described in subsection 707(1) before the expiration of the thirty days`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where at any time prior to the expiration of the thirty days referred to in subsection (1), a witness being detained in custody as described in that subsection applies to be brought before a judge of a court described therein"

-- src:14656 | (3) If the judge before whom a witness is brought under this section is not satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified, the judge shall order them to be discharged or to be released on recognizance, with or without sureties, so that the witness will appear and give evidence when required. However, if the judge is satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified, the judge may order their continued detention until they do what is required of them under section 550 or the trial is concluded, or until they appear and give evidence when required, except that the total period of detention of the witness from the time they were first detained in custody shall not in any case exceed 90 days.
@ref s 707(3) not satisfied (src:14656-14656)
GIVEN `the witness is brought before a judge under section 707` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is not satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 707(3) the judge must order the witness to be discharged or to be released on recognizance, with or without sureties` MEANS
    IF `the witness is brought before a judge under section 707` AND `the judge is not satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge before whom a witness is brought under this section is not satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified"

-- 707(3), second sentence: "may order their continued detention until they do what is required under section 550 or the trial is concluded, or until they appear and give evidence when required,
-- except that the total period of detention ... shall not in any case exceed 90 days".
-- @tag grant=flip
-- @tag grant=closed
-- src:14656 | (3) If the judge before whom a witness is brought under this section is not satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified, the judge shall order them to be discharged or to be released on recognizance, with or without sureties, so that the witness will appear and give evidence when required. However, if the judge is satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified, the judge may order their continued detention until they do what is required of them under section 550 or the trial is concluded, or until they appear and give evidence when required, except that the total period of detention of the witness from the time they were first detained in custody shall not in any case exceed 90 days.
@ref s 707(3) continued detention (src:14656-14656)
GIVEN `the witness is brought before a judge under section 707` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total period of detention of the witness from the time they were first detained in custody, in days, if the detention is continued` IS A NUMBER
      `the witness has done what is required of them under section 550, or the trial is concluded, or the witness has appeared and given evidence when required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the witness is brought before a judge under section 707`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge before whom a witness is brought under this section"
        IF NOT `the judge is satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge is satisfied that the continued detention of the witness is justified"
        IF `the total period of detention of the witness from the time they were first detained in custody, in days, if the detention is continued` GREATER THAN 90
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the total period of detention of the witness from the time they were first detained in custody shall not in any case exceed 90 days"
        IF `the witness has done what is required of them under section 550, or the trial is concluded, or the witness has appeared and given evidence when required`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until they do what is required of them under section 550 or the trial is concluded, or until they appear and give evidence when required"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 708 -- Contempt`

-- "without lawful excuse" limits the offence in its own wording: a person with a lawful excuse is NOT COVERED here (the guide's rule for "without").
-- src:14658 | 708 (1) A person who, being required by law to attend or remain in attendance for the purpose of giving evidence, fails, without lawful excuse, to attend or remain in attendance accordingly is guilty of contempt of court.
@ref s 708(1) (src:14658-14658)
GIVEN `the person is required by law to attend or remain in attendance for the purpose of giving evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to attend or remain in attendance accordingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 708(1) the person is guilty of contempt of court` MEANS
    IF `the person is required by law to attend or remain in attendance for the purpose of giving evidence` AND `the person fails to attend or remain in attendance accordingly` AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who, being required by law to attend or remain in attendance for the purpose of giving evidence, fails, without lawful excuse, to attend or remain in attendance accordingly is guilty of contempt of court"

