§§ `Section 708.1 -- Electronically transmitted copies`

-- src:14666 | 708.1 A copy of a summons, warrant or subpoena transmitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 708.1 (src:14666-14666)
GIVEN `the copy is a copy of a summons, warrant or subpoena` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy was transmitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 708.1 the copy has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of the Criminal Code` MEANS
    IF `the copy is a copy of a summons, warrant or subpoena` AND `the copy was transmitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of this Act"
